judge_raw_output:
The analyzer shows the search is being pulled toward the failure hyperplane by nominal_performance (nominal mean 0.5044 vs robust mean 0.3900) while cliff_margin is too weak (mean 0.0608, weight 0.5) and many designs remain close to or crossing the cliff (cliff worst -0.1298, robust best only 0.4724). This looks like an objective-weighting problem: the optimizer is rewarded for risky nominal gains that don't survive tolerances. I will change the objective weights to prioritize robust_performance_mc and cliff_margin and remove nominal_performance to remove the conflicting incentive.

