  "intervention_target": "objective",
  "rationale": "Nominal mean = 0.5044 vs robust mean = 0.3900 (gap ~0.11). cliff_margin mean = 0.0608 with weight 0.5; many candidates lie close to or beyond the failure boundary (cliff worst = -0.1298). Increasing the priority of robust_performance_mc and cliff_margin and removing nominal_performance will favor designs with higher expected performance under the stated manufacturing noise and reduce risky pushes toward the cliff.",
  "proposed_change": {
    "ops": [
      {"op": "drop", "name": "nominal_performance"},
