The analyzer shows the population is overly conservative: every candidate has positive cliff_margin (min 0.0848) and cliff_margin mean rose by +0.0357 while robust_performance_mc is noisy (mean 0.4435, std 0.0591, best 0.5092). This suggests the cliff_margin objective is pulling search away from the high-performing boundary region. I will make a minimal objective-level change to rebalance safety vs. performance: add nominal_performance (to bias search toward intrinsically high-performing designs) and reduce cliff_margin weight so the optimizer can safely explore closer to the failure boundary once nominal signals support it.

